; 06-no-big-integers.l0 -- int is the only integer, and it has 64 bits.
; An exact calculator over 64-bit rationals cannot answer 47,596 of
; 100,000 random lines of integers up to 999, four levels deep
; (../data/exprs.txt). The literal below is a compile error, and there is
; no type it could have been.
;
; The workaround, ../calc/big.l0, is 261 lines of limb arithmetic in
; lists; with it the calculator answers every line, identically to
; Python's Fraction, in 19.8 s against Python's 3.6 s (0.77 s when every
; result past 64 bits is refused instead).
(def two_to_the_64 () int 18446744073709551616)

(def main () int
  (let w (write_line (digits (two_to_the_64))) 0))
